The ordinary and ``python3 -O`` output streams byte-match.  Certificate gates
use explicit exceptions rather than optimization-removable assertions.

Interpretation and scope:

* The first line is an exact coordinate control for the standard positive
  3-form

      phi=e123+e145+e167+e246-e257-e347-e356.

  At x=e7, J_x(v)=x cross v squares to -1 on x-perp.  Using the round
  Levi-Civita connection and the convention N_J=[J,J], the displayed tangent
  pair has N_J(e1,e2)=4e4.  Thus this standard G2-invariant J is not
  integrable.  It says nothing by itself about non-G2-invariant almost-complex
  structures.

* The second line independently rebuilds the parity restriction matrices for
  L_A(X)=AX+XA^T from the integer A in arXiv:2608.20875v1.  Exact rational
  LDL^T pivots prove the symmetric squared norm is below 1196; the printed
  integer skew witness has Rayleigh numerator 64387950, denominator 53836,
  and surplus 94 over 1196.  This verifies the paper's order-seven
  certificate relative to its displayed matrix, not peer review of the
  preprint.

* The zero-padding line closes the direct-sum implication exactly.  For
  diag(A,0_m), each symmetric and skew cross block has the form

      [[0,B],[+/-B^T,0]] -> [[0,AB],[+/-B^T A^T,0]],

  so its norm is the norm of B -> AB.  The seven displayed leading minors of
  1196 I-A^T A are positive, while the old skew witness remains embedded.
  Hence the same strict separator works in every order n>=7.  The value
  ||A||_F^2=1751>1196 is a hostile showing that a crude Frobenius bound cannot
  replace the spectral/Sylvester check.  The order-six case remains open.

* The nonnormality line proves that this A is strongly nonnormal: AA^T-A^TA has full
  rank seven.  A separate elementary argument in the companion synthesis
  proves that every real normal A lies on the conjecture-positive locus.

* The last line decomposes the paper's skew witness under

      Lambda^2(R^7)=Lambda^2_7 + Lambda^2_14

  for the chosen G2 form.  The numbers use upper-triangle two-form norm; full
  matrix Frobenius norms are twice these values.  Both projections are
  nonzero.  The witness is therefore not a pure cross-product direction and
  not an element of g2 for this structure.  The preprint itself chooses no
  positive 3-form and uses no G2-equivariant map.

* The final line gives the matrix Frobenius-norm squares of the paper's A in
  End(R7)=1+27+7+14.  Every channel is nonzero.  This decomposition depends on
  the chosen positive 3-form; it is a diagnostic, not an equivariance claim.
